    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found mathematics cold and distant, more suited to logic than to human experience. My vocational diploma didn’t include much math, and I’ve never felt a deep connection to it. I appreciate its structure, but I see it as separate from the art, philosophy, and emotion I value more in life.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Not really. I don’t feel anxiety about math because I’ve never had to rely on it for survival or daily tasks. My anxiety comes from uncertainty in life, not equations. Math doesn’t trigger me—perhaps because it’s so rigid and doesn’t mirror the fluidity of human thought or emotion.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I didn’t use AI for math learning. I’ve tried a few tools for photography and music, which are more aligned with my interests. Math feels like a foreign language I don’t need to speak. I’m open to learning, but I prefer understanding through experience, not algorithms.",
