    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized explanations, adapt to different learning paces, and make abstract concepts more relatable through real-life analogies. But they should support—not replace—human teachers. For students like me who don’t connect with math, LLMs could offer gentle, non-judgmental guidance, helping reduce fear and build confidence."
